\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces A6 --- Repeated-game cartel folk-theorem. Left: sustainability map over the $(p_d, \delta )$ grid; red cells are configurations where the grim-trigger cartel beats one-shot defection in expected PV (sustainable), white cells are where it does not (collapses). The thick black vertical bars mark the per-row threshold $p_d^\star $. Right: mean cartel lifespan (rounds until first detection) vs.\ $p_d$, one line per discount factor $\delta $. At the realistic $\delta = 0.95$, $p_d^\star \approx 0.10$: protocols must achieve $\ge 10\%$ per-round detection to break repeated-game cartels.}}{30}{figure.caption.52}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cartel-folk}{{9}{30}{A6 --- Repeated-game cartel folk-theorem. Left: sustainability map over the $(p_d, \delta )$ grid; red cells are configurations where the grim-trigger cartel beats one-shot defection in expected PV (sustainable), white cells are where it does not (collapses). The thick black vertical bars mark the per-row threshold $p_d^\star $. Right: mean cartel lifespan (rounds until first detection) vs.\ $p_d$, one line per discount factor $\delta $. At the realistic $\delta = 0.95$, $p_d^\star \approx 0.10$: protocols must achieve $\ge 10\%$ per-round detection to break repeated-game cartels}{figure.caption.52}{}}
